<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chosokabe Kunichika</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1504–1560</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chosokabe Kunichika was a Japanese warlord of Tosa province on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shikoku">Shikoku</a> and head of the Chosokabe clan in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a>. Raised in exile after his father's death in a war among the local families, he recovered the clan castle of Oko and rebuilt Chosokabe power in central Tosa. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chosokabe-motochika">Chosokabe Motochika</a>, who succeeded him in 1560, unified Tosa and went on to conquer most of Shikoku.</p></div>
